            <ArticleTitle>As sales for autoimmune disease drugs go up, donut hole relief is on the way.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>49</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A study published last year in Arthritis &amp; Rheumatology looked at 2,737 formularies for Medicare Part D plans in 50 states and Washington, D.C., from 2013. The researchers found that nearly all plans required coinsurance and that translated into an average out-of-pocket expense of about $2,700.</AbstractText>
